{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "נכחו", :translit "nicho", :gloss "before it"} {:he "כי נכחו יצא", :translit "ki nicho yatza", :gloss "for before it he went out"} {:he "לא ישוב דרך השער אשר בא בו כי נכחו יצא", :translit "lo yashuv derekh ha-sha'ar asher ba vo ki nicho yatza", :gloss "he shall not return by way of the gate through which he came in, for before it he went out"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["נכחו" "כי נכחו יצא"]} {:kind :other, :note "Gezerah shavah linking the two occurrences of נכחו: the entry path differs from the exit path in both contexts."}], :frame {:text "The verse in Ezekiel 44:9 describes the prince who enters by one gate and exits כי נכחו — by way of another, as Ezekiel 44:9 states, 'he shall not return by way of the gate through which he came in.' Ba'al HaTurim applies this principle to Israel's crossing of the sea: the Israelites entered from one side and exited on the other. The midrashic tradition in Pesachim 118b records that just as Israel ascended from one side, so the Egyptians were cast up from the other side, as the Holy One commanded the sea to discharge them on the side through which Israel had departed.", :sources ["Ezekiel 44:9" "Pesachim 118b"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["נכחו" "כי נכחו יצא"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "נכחו", :refs ["Exodus 14:2" "Isaiah 57:2" "Ezekiel 46:9"], :n 3, :lens :exact} {:phrase "כי נכחו יצא", :refs ["Ezekiel 46:9"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive}]} {:kind :other, :note "Gezerah shavah linking the two occurrences of נכחו: the entry path differs from the exit path in both contexts.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:15:40.165020195Z", :model "glm-5.2"}